Reading: the hard rows are not bunched by the half-turn meter.  Their H values remain roughly 0.74-0.92 of the initial near-regular clock top, while the true LRC certificate depends on the anchored origin margin and endpoint clock.

SYNTHESIS
========================================================================================
1. H=1 is the sharp bunched/open-semicircle reading, with tie boundary at max_gap = 1/2.
2. For H>1, H is not determined by max_gap and is not pointwise monotone.
3. H correlates with spread/entropy, but it also sees cyclic arrangement.
4. The two-neighbor safe count at 1/n is extra data, not recoverable from H.
5. LRC needs the half-turn clock plus the anchored endpoint clock.
